body:
@SilentTester73 I think one should start with reading the documentation and try to understand the semantic of the operation. 

For example in case of cosine similarity, it feels like CPU should not have tried to downcast eps to float16, as common dtype is float64. 
But assuming that both inputs are float16, I'm not sure what the expected behavior should be if eps is larger than dtype maximum value. May be it should be silently upcasted to inf,  but I don't think this is a good behavior for all operations, and kind of low priority, as in practice one is unlikely going to call this one with large epsilon values
